Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 31 CLINICAL DATA  Previous fine needle aspiration showed adenocarcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  98    REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  EXTENDING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE POSTERIOR RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  2    CRIBIFORM TYPE WITH NECROSIS AND ASSOCIATED MICROCALCIFICATIONS  APPROACHING THE INKED SURFACE IN SEVERAL AREAS  BREAST  RIGHT   ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEVERAL MICROSCOPIC FOCI  PRESENT WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF INKED SURFACE  NOTE  No definite blood vascular or lymphatic invasion is present  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 18 02                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   I