Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  25 MAY 93 ACCESSIONED ON  25 MAY 93 at 14 33 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast lesion                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  EXTENSIVE  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  90   WITH EXTENSIVE CANCERIZATION OF LOBULES  1 6 CM IN DIAMETER  EXTENDING TO AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SLIDE D  AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  10    2  MICROCALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  Definite lymphatic invasion is not present  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Sigrid Regauer  MD Signed On  28 MAY 93 at 17 59 Staff Pathologist  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                      S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   1   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 372 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 3  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 12     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 u