Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 AUG 98 ACCESSIONED ON  07 AUG 98 at 14 11 CLINICAL DATA  Needle localization                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  SINGLE FOCUS SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION AND AT REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE CLOSEST RESECTION MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  CONFINED TO THE MASS AND PRESENT AT THE RESECTION MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  NOTE  Invasion of lymphatic vessels and blood vessels is not seen  Diagnosis by  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD Signed On  11 AUG 98 at 16 39 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a 