erexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  The sections stained for estrogen and progesterone receptor proteins and HER 2 c erbB 2 do not contain invasive carcinoma  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 14 34 Consulting Pathologist s   MELINDA J  FAN  MD GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm simple mastectomy specimen which is oriented by the surgeon with a short stitch designating  superior   a long stitch designating  lateral  and a double stitch designating  hot spot    intramammary node   There is a overlying REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm tan ellipse of skin with a central unremarkable 3 5cm nipple areolar complex  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm healed scar on the medial aspect of the nipple  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm cavity subjacent to the scar  The cavity has a smooth  hemorrhagic lining  The parenchyma surrounding the cavity is indurated with focal chalky foci  Multiple cysts are present within the tissue between the cavity and deep margin  The cavity comes to 3 0cm from the deep margin  abuts the skin  and is REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE and 17cm from the medial  superior  inferior  and lateral margins respectively  The remaining breast parenchyma is predominately fatty with delicate white fibrous tissues  The tissue adjacent to the lateral margin marked with a double stitch is ragged and hemorrhagic  No lymph nodes are identified directly at the stitch  Within the adjacent hemorrhagic  ragged tissue two possible lymph nodes are identified measuring 1 5cm and 0 7cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Cavity to skin  B D  Cavity  E  Deep margin closest to cavity  F G  Parenchyma from lower outer quadrant  H  Parenchyma from upper outer quadrant  I  Parenchyma from lower inner quadrant  J  Parenchyma from upper inner quadrant  K  Two possible lymph nodes from the lateral aspect  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a 20 x 23 x 3cm mastectomy specimen which is oriented by the surgeon with a short stitch designating  superior  and a long stitch designating  lateral   There is an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 2 7cm unremarkable tan ellipse of skin with a central 3 3cm nipple areolar complex  The specimen is inked black  serially sectioned to reveal grossly unremarkable breast parenchyma  No lesions are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  L N  Upper outer quadrant  O P  Lower outer quadrant  Q R  Lower inner quadrant  Q represents deep margin   S U  Upper inner quadrant  S represents deep margin   Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional tissue upper outer left breast  is a 8 x 7 x 3cm aggregate of fibrofatty breast tissue with no orientation  The specimen is serially sectioned and no masses are identified  Representative sections are submitted in V EE  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm aggregate of adipose tissue within which two lymph nodes are identified measuring 1 5cm and 2 3cm in greatest dimension  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as follows  FF  One whole lymph node  GG  One lymph node bisected  Gross Description by  SHANNON SCHUTZ Resident  RESIDENT FREE SERVICE  MJF      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS D