Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 02 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 19 00 CLINICAL DATA  Invasive breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  EXTENSIVE FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL IN SITU OR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 13 09                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm portion of fibroadipose tissue which has a short suture designating anterior and long suture designating lateral  and a bowtie designating cephalad  The anterior aspect is black inked  the posterior is blue inked  the superior is yellow inked  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm hemorrhagic cavity with adjacent fat necrosis and fibrous tissue consistent with a previous biopsy site which comes to within 0 1cm of the medial  0 3cm of the inferior  1 1cm of the posterior  1 5cm of the anterior  2 0cm of the superior  and lateral margins  Residual tumor is not grossly appreciated  Adjacent to the cavity  a small amount of white fibrous tissue extends to 0 2cm of the anterior margin while the remaining tissue is yellow  lobulated and fatty  Representative sections are submitted sequentially from medial to lateral as follows  A D  Entire medial margin  radial sections  E  Cavity to inferior margin  F  Cavity to anterior inferior margin  G  Cavity to posterior inferior margin  H  Cavity to anterior inferior margin  I  Cavity with adjacent fibrous tissue to posterior margin  J  Fibrous tissue to anterior superior margin  Gross Descri