an pink fibrotic tissue with focal areas of fat necrosis with no discrete masses or lesions grossly appreciated  Representative sections of the exposed cavity are submitted in cassettes A D and the uninvolved superior margin in cassette E and the uninvolved inferior margin in cassette F  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved lateral REMOVED_DATE of cavity  are 2 irregular  unoriented tan yellow to pink lobulated portions of fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  Both portions are serially sectioned to reveal an unremarkable fibrofatty cut surface  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes G H  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin medial REMOVED_DATE of cavity  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm irregular  unoriented tan pink to yellow fibrofatty portion of soft tissue with cauterizing artifact along one aspect  The unoriented specimen is serially sectioned to reveal an unremarkable cut surface  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes I L  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  CHRISTOPHER M  WILLIAM  MD   Ph D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST LEFT  RE EXCISION PART B  BREAST LEFT  LATERAL REMOVED_DATE SHAVED MARGIN  EXCISION PART C  BREAST LEFT  MEDIAL REMOVED_DATE SHAVED MARGIN  EXCISION , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  17 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 10 39 CLINICAL DATA  63 year old with palpable right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 47                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 06 50 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  and unit number only  are 7 cores of soft  tan tissue  ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm which are submitted in toto as A  Gross Description by  Joe Serra Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Najmosama Nikrui  M D  Priscilla Slanetz  M D  Rakesh Jain  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST CORE BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
