Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 14 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  4 CM  INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of the tumor  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 3 OF 13 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor cells transgresses the capsule of one lymph node to slightly invade the axillary fat  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY   ADDITIONAL    THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 08                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right breast tissue  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm  with a skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm with a grossly unremarkable nipple  An attached axillary tail measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  Sectioning reveals a white  hard lesion measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm which grossly approaches the deep margin which is the closest margin to 0 2cm  Section code  AandB  lesion and deep margin C G  representative sections of lesion H L  lymph nodes from axillary tail Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  additional axillary tissue  is a single piece of fatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Submitted in toto in cassette M  Resident  ALEXANDER KRATZ  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael L Grossbard  M D  Simon Powell  M D  Michael J Yaremchuk  M D  PART A  RIGHT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  ADDITIONAL RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODE   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 19 20 CLINICAL DATA  Inflammatory carcinoma  right breast  previous chemotherapy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  SMALL FOCUS  2  FIBROSIS  GLANDULAR ATROPHY  SCAR  CHRONIC INFLAMMATION AND MULTINUCLEATED FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION  CONSISTENT WITH BIOPSY SITE  3  ELEVEN AXILLARY LYMPH NODES WITH SINUS HISTIOCYTOSIS  AND NESTS OF BENIGN APPEARING NEVOMELANOCYTES IN ONE LYMPH NODE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The inked resection margins are negative for carcinoma  A single lymph node shows numerous benign appearing nests of nevomelanocytic cells  This may be observed rarely as an incidental finding  however  the degree of involvement of this lymph node suggests the possibility of metastasis from a blue nevus or other melanocytic proliferation  Drs  Lynn Duncan and Martin Mihm have reviewed the lymph node slides and concur with the interpretation  Diagnosis by  Daniel Rubin  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 21                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in two containers  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  Labeled  Right breast and axillary contents  is a 390 gm  23 x 15 x 3 5cm modified radical mastectomy partially covered by a REMOVED_DATE x 5cm skin ellipse containing a curved  2cm  well healed scar lateral to the areola  A long and a small black suture are attached to the specimen  designating the lateral and superior aspect  respectively  The specimen is inked and sectioned  revealing predominantly lobulated  yellow adipose tissue intermixed with gray white  fibrous breast parenchyma that is slightly firmer and with a gritty consistency in the region below the skin scar  The nipple and areola are unremarkable  The axillary adipose tissue is sectioned  revealing several tan pink  soft  grossly unremarkable lymph nodes measuring up to 1cm in greatest diameter  SECTION CODE  A B   breast and deep resection margin in the area underlying the scar C through G   breast parenchyma in the area underlying the scar H I   random sections from unremarkable breast J   nipple K   skin scar L M   axillary lymph nodes  Labeled  Right additional axillary tissue  is a 1 x 1 x 0 3cm piece of adipose tissue  Sectioning reveals a lymph node most of which has been replaced by fat  The specimen is bisected and submitted entirely in N  Resident  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  AMB GEN SURGICAL   ACC 4 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST WITH AXILLA PART B  RIGHT ADDITIONAL AXILLARY TISSUE   report_end  , Unchecked.
