g of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right breast  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm soft fatty tissue of breast  inked and sectioned to reveal a fibrofatty cut surface  No frozen is done  Representative section submitted in cassettes from A J  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right breast  are two fatty soft fragments of breast measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm respectively  Inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibrofatty scarred surface  No frozen is done  Representative sections are submitted from cassettes K T  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a specimen with two pieces  The first one is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and contains a stellate ill defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan yellow nodule ascending to the margin  Entirely submitted in cassettes from U Z  with a nodule in U  The second fragment measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and is inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable cut surface and is entirely submitted from AA CC  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  with the patient s name and unit number is a fourth specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm in diameter  inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable cut surface  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes DD MM  Resident  ESTHER OLIVA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     G