ed dark red hemorrhagic cavity  located 1 0cm from the lateral  1 3cm from the posterior  1 5cm from the anterior  2 4cm from the inferior  and 4 5cm from the superior margins  The cavity is filled with dark red clotted blood and the walls are slightly indurated and contain a metal clip  The surrounding area is tan yellow to white  rubbery and lobulated  There are numerous cystic nodular areas containing thick tan white pasty material diffusely located throughout this area  This abuts the anterior  posterior and superior margins  comes to 0 5cm from the inferior  0 8cm from the lateral  and 1 0cm from the medial margins  There is a minimum amount of uninvolved tissue consisting of tan yellow to pink unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Medial margin  radially sectioned   B C  Hemorrhagic cavity with anterior and posterior margins  D  Inferior margin  E  Anterior and posterior margins  F  Superior and posterior margins  G  Lateral margin  radially sectioned   P U  Additional sections of parenchyma  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel node hot and blue left axilla  REMOVED_CASE_ID   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm tan pink lymph node with a moderate amount of attached tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue  The specimen is bisected and entirely submitted in cassette H  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional superior nodule  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm unoriented irregular tan yellow to pink rubbery nodule  The specimen is inked black  serially sectioned to reveal a tan yellow homogeneous rubbery cut surface with multiple tan yellow well delineated nodules averaging 0 1cm in diameter and extending to the closest margin of the resection  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassette I  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional medial nodule left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm unoriented  irregular tan yellow to pink nodule  The specimen is inked black  serially sectioned to reveal a tan yellow to white  mottled fibrous cut surface with a few well delineated tan yellow nodules averaging 0 1cm in diameter which extend to the closest margin of resection  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassette J  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional inferior nodule left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan yellow to pink rubbery soft tissue  The specimen is inked black  serially sectioned to reveal an unremarkable cut surface  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassette K  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  lateral nodule left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm irregular tan yellow to pink rubbery nodule  The specimen is inked black  serially sectioned to reveal a tan yellow to pink  slightly fibrotic cut surface  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes L M  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  upper outer quadrant nodule left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm irregular tan yellow to pink rubbery nodule  The specimen is inked black  serially sectioned to reveal a tan pink to yellow fibrotic cut surface with a few well delineated tan yellow nodules averaging 0 1cm in diameter and extending to the black inked closest margin  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes N O  Gross Description by  JENNIFER NASH Resident  RESIDENT FREE SERVICE  MJF                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODE LEFT SENTINEL AXILLA  REMOVED_CASE_ID   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT SUPERIOR NODULE   EXCI