ogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 MAY 95 at 07 15 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are three separate specimens  Labeled  2 o clock   is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm ellipse of skin  excised to a depth of 0 5cm  entirely frozen as FX 1 and submitted in A  Labeled  4 o clock   is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm ellipse of skin  excised to a depth of 0 4cm  entirely frozen as FX 2 and submitted in B  Labeled  6 o clock   is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm ellipse of skin  excised to a depth of 0 4cm  entirely frozen as FX 3 and submitted in C   ADDON AJA  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 10 0cm mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 15 0cm  tan brown  overlying skin ellipse coating a 4 5cm in diameter areola and 1 5cm in diameter nipple  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm mass protrudes the skin surface 2 0cm lateral and slightly inferior to the nipple  The skin overlying this mass is dark brown to black in color  and is focally enfoliated  Specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm well circumscribed tan yel