e greatest dimension is measured from slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   in conjunction with the immunostains performed on deeper levels from this block  BREAST  RIGHT  CEPHALAD MEDIAL MARGIN   EXCISION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SOLID PAPILLARY TYPE  SMALL FOCUS  SEE NOTE  HYALINIZED FIBROADENOMA  NOTE  Using immunoperoxidase methods  the tumor cells express e cadherin but are negative for cytokeratin REMOVED_DATE  consistent with the above interpretation  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL CEPHALAD MARGIN   EXCISION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SOLID PAPILLARY TYPE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Immunostains for myoepithelial and epithelial cell markers  p63  calponin  heavy chain myosin  cytokeratin  fail to disclose definite evidence of invasion  but the results are suboptimal and invasion cannot be entirely excluded  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL CAUDAD MARGIN   EXCISION  NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL LATERAL MARGIN   EXCISION  FOCAL DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL MEDIAL MARGIN   EXCISION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SOLID PAPILLARY TYPE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Immunostains for myoepithelial and epithelial cell markers  p63  calponin  heavy chain myosin  cytokeratin  fail to disclose definite evidence of invasion  but the results are suboptimal and invasion cannot be entirely excluded  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY  SENTINEL  PRIMARY    REMOVED_CASE_ID    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  ONE NODE   NOTE  Keratin positive tumor cells are not identified on three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 immunostained levels  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY  SENTINEL  SECONDARY   355   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  ONE NODE   NOTE  Keratin positive tumor cells are not identified on three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 immunostained levels  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are eight containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  right breast   is an unoriented  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm lumpectomy specimen with a needle localization wire running through the center of the specimen along the 3 9cm axis  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm tan  firm  ovoid mass with a flat  cut edge protrudes through one aspect of the specimen  and is 1 2cm from one long axis end margin and 2 6cm from the other long axis margin  The remainder of the specimen surface is adipose  fragmented  but otherwise grossly unremarkable  The external surface of the specimen is inked black  the firm mass is now removed  and the area underlying it is inked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned along the long axis to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm area consisting of multiple well circumscribed soft  friable tan nodules  of which the largest is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The clip is identified within the largest nodule  This area abuts the black inked margin approximately 0 4cm from the previously described firm mass  and is 0 2cm from the firm mass  and is 0 7cm from the opposing black inked margin  The area is 1 6cm from one end margin  and 1 8cm from the other end margin  Leading towards the soft mass and abutting it is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm fibrous area consistent with biopsy tract  The remaining breast parenchyma is fibroadipose  and grossly unremarkable  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   End margin closest to mass  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Soft nodules to closest black inked margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Soft nodules to opposite margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Largest nodule to closest black inked margin in area of firm mass  with the portion of specimen where the firm mass was removed overinked blue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Further representative sections of soft nodular area   REM