Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON  17 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 12 07 CLINICAL DATA  Focally recurrent breast cancer  Marking stitches  short superior  long lateral                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  SEVERAL SMALL FOCI OF RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 1 OF 3  REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE CLOSEST DEEP MARGIN  2  TWO HEALING BIOPSY CAVITIES  3  FIBROSIS WITH ATYPICAL STROMAL CELLS AND EPITHELIAL CELL ATYPIA  CONSISTENT WITH RADIATION INJURY  4  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN SIX OF SIX LYMPH NODES  IN THE UPPER OUTER QUADRANT OF THE SPECIMEN   Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 16 04                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a 790gm  24 x 18 x 5 0cm right simple mastectomy specimen with an overlying 24 x 10 0cm tan pink skin ellipse  The skin has two black stitches designating the superior and lateral margins  There is a 5 0cm linear healed scar  which comes to 0 4cm of the 5 o clock margin  Also noted is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm areolus with a central unremarkable REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm nipple  The resection margin is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm hemorrhagic cavity in the lower outer quadrant  which comes to 0 4cm of the deep margin  The cavity is surrounded by yellow orange foci consistent with fat necrosis and focally dense grey white fibrous tissue  Within the surrounding fibrous tissue are two silver metal clips  The first and second clips come to REMOVED_DATE and 3 2cm of the deep margin  respectively  Also noted is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm cystic cavity along the superior aspect which contains a tan yellow  soft necrotic substance  The cavity comes to 0 3cm of the deep margin  The remaining cut surface shows focally cystic and gritty grey white fibrous tissue  no discrete mass or other gross abnormality  Sectioning of the upper outer quadrant reveals several tan red rubbery lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 4cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted  SECTION CODE  A D  Hemorrhagic cavity including deep margin as A B D  and including the first silver metal clip as B C  E  Fibrous tissue containing second silver metal clip  F  Necrotic cavity to deep margin  G  Representative fibrous tissue  H    Six whole lymph nodes  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  PAULA ARNELL  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Simon Powell  M D  PART   BREAST RIGHT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  01 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 46 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  MULTIFOCAL  SEE NOTE  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  NOTE  The largest tumor nodule is 0 8cm in diameter  Several additional small foci are also seen  Tumor is present within 0 05cm of several inked margins  No lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is identified  An in situ component is not identified  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 15                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 40 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm mass of breast tissue with localizing wire in place and accompanying specimen x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm white  ill defined nodule approaching to within 0 3cm of an inked surface  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved as frozen  The remaining specimen is submitted entirely in A through G  Resident  Robin E  Kirby  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FXDX  1   LEFT BREAST MASS  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   BREAST LEFT MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
