Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 MAY 98 ACCESSIONED ON  18 MAY 98 at 08 47 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM  PRESENT AT MULTIPLE INKED SURFACES ALONG BROAD FRONTS  SEE NOTE   LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  NOTE  No definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The invasive tumor is present in both biopsy fragments  This the tumor is most likely greater than 1 5cm in greatest dimension  the fragmented nature of the biopsy precludes optimal assessment of total tumor size  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  21 MAY 98 at 11 19                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a 