Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  01 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 06 CLINICAL DATA  Biopsy proven right breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE 3  SEE NOTE  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is seen  The margins are free of tumor  however  carcinoma is present less that 0 1cm from the deep margin  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 12 OF 12 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 49                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 07 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast lump  is an oriented breast resection specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm white gritty lesion 0 2cm from the posterior  closest  margin  Representative sections are submitted as follows  Section code  A and C  lesion with posterior margin D and E  lesion with anterior margin F  representative sections of lesion G  representative section of superior margin H  representative section of lateral margin I  representative section of medial margin J  representative section of inferior margin Note all margins are submitted radially  Separately  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right axillary contents  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue sectioned to reveal numerous lymph nodes  representative sections of which are submitted in cassettes K O  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   POSITIVE FOR CARCINOMA  MARGINS NEGATIVE  O R  Resident  IVANA DELALLE  MD  PHD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
