Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 57 CLINICAL DATA  82 year old female post menopausal  with mammographic changes in left upper outer quadrant suspicious for carcinoma  Left breast biopsy was diagnosed as infiltrating ductal carcinoma  No palpable adenopathy  Now for left modified radical mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  1  BIOPSY SITE WITH FIBROSIS  FAT NECROSIS  CHRONIC INFLAMMATION AND HEMOSIDERIN LADEN MACROPHAGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES INCLUDING FIBROSIS  CYST FORMATION  APOCRINE METAPLASIA  AND DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  3  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 17 OF 17 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Fiona M  Graeme Cook  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 22                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a 885 gram mastectomy specimen  21 x 15 x 3 5cm with a 19 x 11cm skin ellipse with a central 4 5cm in diameter unremarkable areola with a 1 2cm in diameter central unremarkable nipple  6 2cm superior to the areolar margin and 2 7cm from the apex of the skin ellipse is a 3 5cm long recent incision with a suture at one end  Attached to the apex of the specimen is a 7 x 7 x 1 5cm axillary lymph node dissection  The breast is inked and sectioned to reveal a 2 5cm in diameter biopsy cavity lined by smooth  tan  focally hemorrhagic tissue which is surrounded by granular yellow and red tissue  0 5cm from the closest deep resection margin and 8cm from the closest lateral resection margin  The remainder of the breast is remarkable only for fibrous areas containing up to 0 4cm in diameter cysts  Section Code  A B  biopsy cavity with closest deep resection margin  C D  additional sections of biopsy cavity  E F  representative sections of breast distant from biopsy cavity  G  skin with scar overlying biopsy cavity  H  representative section of nipple  I  skin with closest lateral resection margin  J V  axillary lymph nodes  Resident  Jeoffry Brennick  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  David William Rattner  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST and LEFT AXILLARY NODES   report_end  , Unchecked.
